-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">9</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":9,\"repo\":\"marcodiniz/ABlazorPong\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/last-commit/marcodiniz/ABlazorPong?style=flat-square&#x26;cacheSeconds=86400\" alt=\"last commit\"> A classic Pong in Blazor WebAssembly, with sounds, without a single line of Javascript.  <a href=\"https://marcodiniz.github.io/ABlazorPong/\">Demo</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T17:39:08.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"edm00se/awesome-board-games","categoryHTML":"<h2>Party</h2>","itemHTML":"<h3><a href=\"https://boardgamegeek.com/boardgame/242483/noir\">Noir</a></h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Noir is a \"denouement\" game that lasts only a few minutes per round. The \"denouement mechanic\" is a special type of storytelling game, where the key elements of the stories events are determined by the game, then the players must weave them together in the most inventive of ways.\nNoir is packed with a grim cast of Femme Fatales, gum shoe P.I.s, mean Mobsters and hardened Hit Men. The play throws up stories which are by turns dark, hilarious, inventive and always, always memorable.\nAt the bitter end the best denouement of the game wins!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><img src=\"https://cf.geekdo-images.com/4gaw7uVUCijAZa5bnZP84Q__itemrep/img/iymr5JN2rzqoDvm7soJFk0IvquI=/fit-in/246x300/filters:strip_icc()/pic3941376.png\" alt=\"Noir game image\"></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"right\">Players</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Min. Age</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Time</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\">3 - 6</td>\n<td align=\"right\">10+</td>\n<td align=\"right\">10-60m</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T13:18:04.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"ecohealthalliance/awesome-parasite","categoryHTML":"<h2>Databases</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.mgc.ac.cn/cgi-bin/ZOVER/main.cgi\">Zover</a> - A conglomeration of the previous bat (<a href=\"https://github.com/ecohealthalliance/awesome-parasite/blob/master/www.mgc.ac.cn/DBatVir\">DBatVir</a>) and rodent virus (<a href=\"http://www.mgc.ac.cn/DRodVir/\">DRodVir</a>) databases with the addition of mosquito- and tick- borne viruses. Database is described <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/nar/advance-article/doi/10.1093/nar/gkab862/6389491?login=true\">here</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T13:04:03.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"kdeldycke/awesome-falsehood","categoryHTML":"<h2>Software Engineering</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://scribe.rip/p/what-every-software-engineer-should-know-about-search-27d1df99f80d\">What every software engineer should know about search</a> - A better sourced article on the difficulty of implementing search engines.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T11:25:42.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"academic/awesome-datascience","categoryHTML":"<h2>Books</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://artint.info/index.html\">Artificial Intelligence: Foundations of Computational Agents, 2nd Edition</a> - Free HTML version</li>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T10:23:55.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"avelino/awesome-go","categoryHTML":"<h2>Websites</h2><h3>Tutorials</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/golang-tutorial-list-free-courses-learn-go-programming-language/\">Golang Tutorial Guide</a> - A List of Free Courses to Learn the Go Programming Language</li>","updatedAt":"2021-10-18T08:51:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"matteocrippa/awesome-swift","categoryHTML":"<h2>Libs</h2><h4>Alert</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/BastiaanJansen/To